## 3. Storage & Infrastructure Ceilings

Here is a summary of the remaining infrastructure limits and their projected time-to-failure at a 2,000 request/day load:

| Service | Plan | Limit | Projected Time to Failure (at 2k/day) | Recommended Action |
|---------|------|-------|----------------------------------------|--------------------|
| **Supabase** | Free | 500MB DB Storage | **~14 Months** | Write a cron-job to auto-delete `SiteTraffic` logs older than 30 days. |
| **Cloudinary**| Free | 25GB Storage | **Infinite** (Requires >1M images) | None. 100% Production Ready. |
| **Render** | Free | 15m Idle Sleep | **Immediate (UX Issue)** | Use a free tool like UptimeRobot to ping the server every 14 minutes. |

## Conclusion
To run a massive B2B operation for absolutely $0, the current architecture is flawless up to **3,000 daily active requests**. Once traffic crosses the 5,000 daily mark, you will mathematically be forced to upgrade Render to the $7/mo Starter Tier to prevent memory crashes.
